# WCPOS UI design rules

The rules themselves live in `CODING_STANDARDS.md` § Design — read that section before you draw a mockup, build a screen, touch a component, or review a UI diff. `/code-review` enforces it on the diff; a PR that breaks a rule needs a stated reason in its body.

## Who is standing in front of it

A cashier at a counter, standing, arm's length from a shared tablet, under shop lighting, with a
customer waiting. Sometimes a stall-holder who last opened the app four months ago. Judge every
screen at 5 pm with a queue: can the next action be found in under a second without reading?

## The type floor

Text a cashier reads is never under 12 px in any step (`text-xs` is the floor). `text-2xs` (11 px)
is only for glyph-like text: avatar initials, badge counts. There is no `text-3xs`.
